      "side": 0,
      "message": "\u003e Is there any other corner case other than:\n\u003e \n\u003e link to patch-sets using the change number prefix\n\u003e link to comments using the change number prefix\n\nFor sure we need to cover these 2 cases:\n* patch range suffix [1] (see also your comment here [3])\n* patch number suffix [2]\n\nThe reason why I ended up with a borader expression is to cover all the cases we couldn\u0027t think of with a trainling segment.\n\nI have now realised this can be probelmatic for projects containing numbers.\n\n[1]: https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/346618792\n[2]: https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/346377876\n[3]: https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/390983/comment/5b619cca_3433c3e3/",
      "parentUuid": "c5dc30b2_a7014cf8",
